      "evidence": "The interviewer repeatedly used long, complex, and formal phrasing (e.g., 'Apart from any stimulant prescribed to you and taken as directed, have you ever used stimulants nonmedically...') which consistently confused the patient."
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "category": "efficiency",
      "evidence": "The interviewer frequently repeated the entire questionnaire item, including the full list of options, when the patient expressed confusion, rather than simplifying the question or focusing on the core inquiry."
